00:40:09.591 --> 00:40:13.671
a perfect representation of the mood this game is&nbsp;
trying to convey throughout the whole game we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:13.671 --> 00:40:18.071
been meeting with npcs of all kinds some with&nbsp;
goals and others without but none of them have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:18.071 --> 00:40:23.191
managed to touch my heart in a way that solaire&nbsp;
and siegmeyer did both of them had a goal in mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:23.191 --> 00:40:27.511
one wants to find his sunlight and the other&nbsp;
wants to explore the world but both are stuck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:27.511 --> 00:40:31.831
sigmar always seems to be getting himself caught&nbsp;
in some situation whether that be a locked gate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:31.831 --> 00:40:37.031
he can enter or a poison swap he can cross and&nbsp;
solaire can find his sunlight they both willingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:37.031 --> 00:40:41.271
became undead in order to achieve their goals and&nbsp;
it tore me apart to hear that sigmar couldn't see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:41.271 --> 00:40:45.511
it through sigmar prides himself on being a knight&nbsp;
of catarina and that he can handle all of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:45.511 --> 00:40:50.151
troubles on his own but with my help i showed&nbsp;
him that he wasn't a worthy knight after all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:50.151 --> 00:40:54.311
and that he always needed someone to rescue him&nbsp;
more often than not in these games your assistance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:54.311 --> 00:40:57.831
will lead to their death so it's either converse&nbsp;
with them and enjoy their company knowing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:57.831 --> 00:41:01.671
they will die because of you or distance yourself&nbsp;
from them knowing that while it hurts it's better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:01.671 --> 00:41:05.991
that they get to live another day npcs of these&nbsp;
games will usually end up achieving a terrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:05.991 --> 00:41:10.711
fate but this sadness makes the few times a happy&nbsp;
outcome occurs all the better solaire wasn't able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:10.711 --> 00:41:14.951
to find sunlight of his own he became depressed&nbsp;
and wondered if this journey was really worth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:14.951 --> 00:41:19.991
taking conveying the tone of the entire game is&nbsp;
our journey and our struggle really worth it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:19.991 --> 00:41:24.471
the end which is why i owed it to him to make it&nbsp;
right it may not be the actual sun but the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:24.471 --> 00:41:30.510
flame could be considered the sun so for one final&nbsp;
time i summoned solaire and we took down lord gwyn

00:41:53.991 --> 00:41:59.911
gwyn's theme has such a fitting tune all these&nbsp;
bosses have these intense sounds with loud music&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:59.911 --> 00:42:05.511
but gwyn's is such a simple piano it's not intense&nbsp;
it's almost sad in a way that the most powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:05.511 --> 00:42:09.271
man in the world has been reduced to nothing&nbsp;
and what was supposed to be a glorious fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:09.271 --> 00:42:13.351
between two warriors really isn't it makes it&nbsp;
all the more worse when you realize that gwyn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:13.351 --> 00:42:17.911
can be parried and once you nail this timing down&nbsp;
this fight is a cake walk further showing how far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:17.911 --> 00:42:22.471
from grace he has truly fallen with gwyn defeated&nbsp;
we can now choose our ending but we aren't the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:22.471 --> 00:42:26.551
only one who's able to choose since we managed to&nbsp;
bring solaire all the way to the end of the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:26.551 --> 00:42:31.431
he was able to also fight gwyn in his own world&nbsp;
thanks to the convoluted timelines of dark souls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:31.431 --> 00:42:36.631
and it is canonized that he succeeded and linked&nbsp;
the flame in his own world he became the sunlight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:36.631 --> 00:42:40.951
he was searching for and that might be one of&nbsp;
the greatest endings in the entire franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:40.951 --> 00:42:45.511
but while solaire linked the flame that doesn't&nbsp;
mean we have to if we choose the age of fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:45.511 --> 00:42:50.711
the world continues we rekindle the flame and use&nbsp;
ourselves as kindling to continue this age of fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:50.711 --> 00:42:55.351
if we instead choose to leave we let the flame&nbsp;
extinguish itself we join the primordial serpents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:55.351 --> 00:42:59.911
including kaathe and probably frampt and usher&nbsp;
in an age of dark one where humanity is at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:59.911 --> 00:43:04.471
the top and we ourselves are the ruler at least&nbsp;
that's what we think will happen like many plots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:04.471 --> 00:43:08.311
in the souls series this is once again left up&nbsp;
to interpretation we only get to see the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:08.311 --> 00:43:13.351
beginning of our choice so anything after is just&nbsp;
pure speculation who knows what will happen after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:13.351 --> 00:43:16.471
and who knows if our choice was really the&nbsp;
correct one that's always been up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:16.471 --> 00:43:20.391
player to decide but i've always felt that these&nbsp;
endings are about comfort do we stay comfortable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:20.391 --> 00:43:24.151
knowing that in the age of fire we aren't on&nbsp;
top and might be mistreated due to our lack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:24.151 --> 00:43:27.671
strength or do we take the risk and see what the&nbsp;
age of dark is about one thing to note though is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:27.671 --> 00:43:31.671
the circumstances regarding these endings fram&nbsp;
says that the undead curse will be cured if we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:31.671 --> 00:43:35.511
go with the age of fire and not even kaathe says&nbsp;
anything about this when we talk with him about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:35.511 --> 00:43:39.671
it so does that mean that we'll stay undead or&nbsp;
at least still have the risk of going hollow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:39.671 --> 00:43:43.991
in the age of dark furthermore the age of fire&nbsp;
was a time ruled by the gods and they did what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:43.991 --> 00:43:48.551
they could to keep it that way but we killed&nbsp;
them everyone in anor londo that is a god is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:48.551 --> 00:43:53.191
either dead or gone gwyndolin is the only one&nbsp;
that canonically lives thanks to dark souls 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:53.191 --> 00:43:57.751
so even though an age of fire can be seen as the&nbsp;
age of gods that might not be true anymore as we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:57.751 --> 00:44:02.071
took care of most of them so there is positives&nbsp;
and negatives both ways and that's really been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:02.071 --> 00:44:05.911
the point there's never going to be a clear&nbsp;
answer it's just whatever you think is right as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:05.911 --> 00:44:10.151
for me i think an age of dark is the proper way&nbsp;
to go as we said in the intro the world of dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:10.151 --> 00:44:14.391
souls is like a set of operations things come&nbsp;
and things go and the age of dark should have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:14.391 --> 00:44:18.551
followed after the age of fire but due to gwen&nbsp;
breaking the rules of the world that didn't happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:18.551 --> 00:44:23.111
so i think in an attempt to set things back on&nbsp;
track before further destruction an age of dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:23.111 --> 00:44:26.951
is the way to go regardless of what happens in&nbsp;
this age of dark at the very least things will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:26.951 --> 00:44:31.511
transition back to the way it was supposed to be&nbsp;
however that might not be the actual ending given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:31.511 --> 00:44:35.831
the future titles some have debated on proper&nbsp;
endings and given the status of dark souls 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:35.831 --> 00:44:40.631
linking the flame i think is the real ending and&nbsp;
is definitely the most agreed upon as just about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:40.631 --> 00:44:44.871
every person in this game will speak about linking&nbsp;
the flame we only hear about the age of dark from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:44.871 --> 00:44:49.511
kaathe who we have to jump through several hoops to&nbsp;
just even meet i can almost guarantee someone has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:49.511 --> 00:44:52.951
gone throughout the entire game and didn't even&nbsp;
know that an age of dark was the real option&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:52.951 --> 00:44:57.511
because of how hidden it is and while it's not my&nbsp;
preferred ending continuing the age of fire would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:57.511 --> 00:45:02.791
set in motion numerous events for us to discover&nbsp;
dark souls 1 was a fantastic experience from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:02.791 --> 00:45:07.351
start to finish and while the road was a little&nbsp;
